  "ui_tests_run": false,
  "changes": [
    "WorkspaceColorPreset and WorkspaceEmojiPreset are typed Rust FormCommand variants with Workspace panel ownership. bind_appearance_preset admits only catalogue-valid indices on private form action nodes; generic command init cannot bypass indexed validation and existing bindings cannot change semantic target.",
    "Rust appearance_command_target resolves typed command/index to the canonical color or Unicode emoji and rejects unrelated commands/out-of-range indices. Native preset adapters retain no value-capturing callback in Rust mode; BindAppearancePreset uses the common weak shell dispatcher. Views retains the original callbacks.",
    "Preset activation passes shared Rust epoch/lease/enable admission after activation observers and actual visible settings widget/tree guards before the native workspace color/emoji service. Platform drawing, glyph/text/AX projections and custom editor behavior remain unchanged.",
    "Six new Rust tests cover full catalogue mapping/panel/metadata, invalid index and generic-init rejection, immutable bindings, disabled/retired/wrong model admission, unrelated commands and deferred-ticket cancellation. Two compiled browser cases cover all ten presets with stable node IDs and observer-driven workspace retargeting. No UI tests ran."
  ],
  "deferred_gui_cases": [
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.AppearanceCommandsResolveAllPresetsWithStableActionNodes",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.AppearanceCommandObserverCannotRetargetPresetToAnotherWorkspace",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.AppearanceActionHostsKeyboardAXColorAndCancelledClip",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.FormCommandModelsCoverPreferencesWorkspaceProfilesAndImport"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No UI/browser tests, physical input, preview restart/repackaging or manual acceptance. Compilation does not prove keyboard/pointer/AX, visuals, actual native event ordering, workspace-switch cancellation, persistence or parity.",
    "This moves preset semantic targets and callback admission to Rust. Native RustActionView glyph/color/label projection and AppearanceRow containers/layout application/window/AX services remain adapters. Arbitrary color/emoji editor callbacks still use the established validated native service path.",
    "Existing workspace selection cancellation and native observer/widget checks supply context fences; native delivery acceptance is deferred. Application workspace identity, write authorization, appearance persistence and normalization remain in native services.",
    "Complete form status/busy/managed and editor/text ownership, residual popup/action inventory, sidebar split hierarchy, wider keyed reconciliation and bulk UI/manual/performance/release acceptance remain open. Deferred split work remains locally in build/sidebar-pair-deferred-2026-10-27.patch.",
    "No CPU/GPU/presentation or memory gain is claimed. Catalogue/target conversion costs are unmeasured. No target/dependency/license change; frozen UI-lab bootstrap/network inputs exclude current-main network policy."
  ],
